# discovery.u — the categories that are about not knowing yet: a hypothesis, its rivals, the
# experiment that separates them, the law that comes out, and the gap nobody had noticed.
#
# `experiment` items are `name | what it would show if true | what it would show if false`, which
# is the shape `epistemic.EpistemicCompiler` needs to call an observation discriminating: an
# experiment both hypotheses predict the same answer to is not an experiment.

# ============================ hypothesis formation ============================================= #
@record hypothesis plant_wilting
domain     = biology
observation_text = a potted plant on a sunny windowsill has wilted overnight
hypotheses = it ran out of water | 0.4 ;; the roots are rotting from too much water | 0.25 ;; it was scorched by direct sun | 0.2 ;; it is cold damage from the window | 0.15
unknown    = which of the four is doing it
text       = a wilted plant has at least four ordinary explanations and they call for opposite actions.

@record hypothesis engine_wont_start
domain     = technology
observation_text = a car turns over slowly and does not start on a cold morning
hypotheses = the battery is weak | 0.45 ;; the starter motor is failing | 0.2 ;; the fuel is not reaching the engine | 0.2 ;; the oil is too thick for the temperature | 0.15
text       = slow cranking narrows it, and does not settle it.

@record hypothesis bread_did_not_rise
domain     = everyday
observation_text = a loaf came out dense and flat
hypotheses = the yeast was dead | 0.4 ;; the water was too hot and killed it | 0.25 ;; there was too much salt against the yeast | 0.2 ;; it was not left long enough | 0.15
text       = four causes, one symptom.

@record hypothesis network_is_slow
domain     = computing
observation_text = a service answers in two seconds where it used to answer in eighty milliseconds
hypotheses = a database query lost its index | 0.35 ;; the cache is cold after a deploy | 0.3 ;; an upstream dependency is slow | 0.2 ;; the machine is out of memory and swapping | 0.15
text       = the same symptom is produced by four different failures.

@record hypothesis fever_after_travel
domain     = medicine
observation_text = a traveller returns from a tropical region with a cyclic fever
hypotheses = malaria | 0.4 ;; influenza | 0.25 ;; a bacterial infection | 0.2 ;; dengue | 0.15
note       = the cycle is the feature that raises the first one above the ordinary base rate.
text       = the pattern of the fever is doing the work, not the fever.

# ============================ rival hypotheses and the experiment that splits them ============= #
@record rival_hypotheses plant_wilting_split
domain     = biology
hypotheses = it ran out of water | 0.5 ;; the roots are rotting | 0.5
experiment = push a finger into the soil | dry soil means it ran out of water | wet soil means the roots are rotting ;; lift the pot and feel its weight | light means dry | heavy means waterlogged
outcome    = push a finger into the soil | the soil is soaking wet
text       = one observation, and the two explanations predict opposite results, which is what makes it worth doing.

@record rival_hypotheses engine_split
domain     = technology
hypotheses = the battery is weak | 0.5 ;; the starter motor is failing | 0.5
experiment = switch on the headlights and watch them while cranking | they dim badly, so it is the battery | they stay bright, so it is the starter
outcome    = switch on the headlights and watch them while cranking | the lights stayed bright
text       = the lights and the starter share the battery, which is why this splits them.

@record rival_hypotheses fever_split
domain     = medicine
hypotheses = malaria | 0.5 ;; influenza | 0.5
experiment = examine a blood film under a microscope | parasites visible means malaria | no parasites means it is not malaria
outcome    = examine a blood film under a microscope | parasites were seen
text       = the test is chosen because the two answers point different ways, not because it is easy.

@record rival_hypotheses network_split
domain     = computing
hypotheses = a query lost its index | 0.5 ;; the cache is cold | 0.5
experiment = run the same request twice in a row | the second is fast, so it was the cache | both are slow, so it is the query
outcome    = run the same request twice in a row | both requests were slow
text       = a cold cache is warm the second time and a missing index is not.

@record rival_hypotheses bread_split
domain     = everyday
hypotheses = the yeast was dead | 0.5 ;; the dough was not left long enough | 0.5
experiment = stir the same yeast into warm sugar water and wait ten minutes | it foams, so the yeast was alive | it stays flat, so the yeast was dead
outcome    = stir the same yeast into warm sugar water and wait ten minutes | it stayed flat
text       = testing the ingredient on its own separates it from how it was used.

@record rival_hypotheses light_nature
domain     = physics
context    = the historical case where one experiment settled two centuries of argument
hypotheses = light is a stream of particles | 0.5 ;; light is a wave | 0.5
experiment = shine light through two narrow slits onto a screen | two bright bands means particles | many alternating bands means a wave
outcome    = shine light through two narrow slits onto a screen | many alternating bright and dark bands appeared
text       = interference fringes are what a wave does and what a stream of pellets does not.

# ============================ experiment design ================================================= #
@record experiment_design does_water_drive_growth
domain     = biology
question   = does watering cause the growth, or does something that comes with watering cause it
experiment = give matched plants different measured amounts of water and nothing else different | growth tracks water, so water drives it | growth is flat, so something else does
outcome    = give matched plants different measured amounts of water and nothing else different | growth rose with water
note       = matched plants and one thing varied. everything else held is what makes the answer about water.
text       = vary one thing, hold the rest, and measure.

@record experiment_design placebo_control
domain     = medicine
question   = is the improvement from the drug or from being treated at all
experiment = give one matched group the drug and the other an identical dummy | the drug group improves more, so it is the drug | both improve equally, so it is not
outcome    = give one matched group the drug and the other an identical dummy | the drug group improved more
text       = the control exists because getting better is something people do anyway.

@record experiment_design blind_taste
domain     = everyday
question   = does the expensive coffee actually taste different
experiment = serve both unlabelled in identical cups | the expensive one is picked out reliably | the picks are no better than chance
outcome    = serve both unlabelled in identical cups | the picks were no better than chance
text       = the label is the thing that has to be removed for the question to be about the taste.

@record experiment_design ab_test_latency
domain     = computing
question   = does the new index make the endpoint faster in production
experiment = route half the traffic to each version and compare the median | the new half is faster, so the index helps | the halves match, so it does not
outcome    = route half the traffic to each version and compare the median | the new half was forty percent faster
text       = the two halves see the same traffic at the same time, which is what a before and after cannot promise.

@record experiment_design does_heavier_fall_faster
domain     = physics
question   = do heavier objects fall faster than light ones
experiment = drop a heavy and a light ball of the same shape together in still air | the heavy one lands first | they land together
outcome    = drop a heavy and a light ball of the same shape together in still air | they landed together
note       = same shape, so air resistance is held rather than confounded with weight.
text       = matching the shape is what makes this a test of weight.

# ============================ discovery: readings to a law ===================================== #
@record discovery boyle_from_readings
domain     = physics
context    = seven readings of a gas at constant temperature, and the pattern in them
variables  = volume | pressure
series     = 1 | 600 ;; 1.5 | 400 ;; 2 | 300 ;; 3 | 200 ;; 4 | 150 ;; 5 | 120 ;; 6 | 100
law        = volume | causes | pressure | -1
concept    = the product of pressure and volume is constant
text       = pressure halves when volume doubles, and the product stays at six hundred throughout.

@record discovery hooke_from_readings
domain     = physics
variables  = extension | force
series     = 0 | 0 ;; 2 | 5 ;; 4 | 10 ;; 6 | 15 ;; 8 | 20 ;; 10 | 25
law        = extension | causes | force | 1
concept    = force is proportional to extension while the spring is elastic
text       = every extra two centimetres adds the same five newtons.

@record discovery lapse_rate_from_readings
domain     = earth_science
variables  = altitude | temperature
series     = 0 | 15 ;; 1 | 8.5 ;; 2 | 2 ;; 3 | -4.5 ;; 4 | -11 ;; 5 | -17.5
law        = altitude | causes | temperature | -1
concept    = temperature falls by about six and a half degrees for each kilometre of altitude
text       = the drop is the same for every kilometre, which is what makes it a rate.

@record discovery pendulum_from_readings
domain     = physics
variables  = length | period
series     = 0.25 | 1 ;; 1 | 2 ;; 2.25 | 3 ;; 4 | 4 ;; 6.25 | 5
law        = length | causes | period | 1
concept    = the period goes with the square root of the length, so four times the length doubles it
text       = quadrupling the length doubles the period, which is a square root and not a proportion.

@record scientific_law ohm_from_readings
domain     = physics
variables  = voltage | current
series     = 1 | 0.2 ;; 2 | 0.4 ;; 4 | 0.8 ;; 6 | 1.2 ;; 10 | 2
law        = voltage | causes | current | 1
concept    = current is voltage divided by resistance, and the resistance here is five ohms
text       = the ratio of voltage to current is the same five at every reading.

@record scientific_law demand_from_readings
domain     = economics
variables  = price | demand
series     = 20 | 112 ;; 30 | 98 ;; 40 | 84 ;; 50 | 70 ;; 60 | 56 ;; 70 | 42
law        = price | causes | demand | -1
concept    = demand falls by a fixed amount for each rise in price over this range
text       = every ten rupees costs fourteen kilograms of sales.

@record scientific_law dose_response
domain     = medicine
variables  = dose | relief
series     = 0 | 0 ;; 50 | 2.3 ;; 100 | 3.2 ;; 200 | 4.5 ;; 400 | 6.4
law        = dose | causes | relief | 1
concept    = relief rises with the square root of the dose, so doubling it does not double the effect
text       = the returns fall off, which is why the fourth doubling buys much less than the first.

# ============================ unknown unknowns ================================================== #
@record unknown_unknown scurvy_before_vitamins
domain     = medicine
belief     = sailors fall ill on long voyages because the sea air is bad
anomaly    = ships carrying citrus had healthy crews on the same route and the same air
missing    = a required nutrient that fresh food supplies and salt rations do not
text       = the model had no slot for a substance a body needs and cannot make, so the citrus result looked like luck.

@record unknown_unknown mercury_orbit_precession
domain     = astronomy
belief     = newtonian gravity accounts for every planetary orbit
anomaly    = mercury's orbit precesses by a small amount that no planet accounts for
missing    = a theory in which mass curves spacetime rather than pulling across it
text       = an unexplained residue that would not shrink was the signature of a missing theory rather than a missing planet.

@record unknown_unknown childbed_fever
domain     = medicine
belief     = childbed fever is caused by bad air in the ward
anomaly    = the ward staffed by doctors coming from the dissection room had far more deaths than the one staffed by midwives
missing    = an agent carried on hands from one body to another
text       = the difference between two wards in the same building could not be air.

@record unknown_unknown ulcer_bacterium
domain     = medicine
belief     = no bacterium can survive the acid of the stomach
anomaly    = ulcers healed on antibiotics, which should do nothing to a stress disorder
missing    = an organism that neutralises acid around itself
text       = the treatment working was the anomaly that named the missing concept.

@record unknown_unknown background_hiss
domain     = astronomy
belief     = the antenna noise is a fault in the equipment
anomaly    = the hiss was the same in every direction, at every hour, in every season
missing    = radiation left over from the early universe
text       = a fault points somewhere. this pointed everywhere, which is what said it was not a fault.

# ============================ curiosity ========================================================= #
@record curiosity what_else_causes_growth
domain     = biology
unknown    = whether anything besides water is driving the growth
question   = does anything else cause growth
note       = the question `assume.AssumptionMiner` asks of any arrow held as if it were the only one.
text       = one measured cause does not establish that it is the only cause.

@record curiosity is_the_arrow_backwards
domain     = biology
unknown    = whether the direction of the water and growth arrow is settled
question   = could growth cause water instead
text       = five readings of two variables cannot tell which drives which, and that is a real gap rather than a silly one.

@record curiosity condition_on_the_law
domain     = chemistry
unknown    = whether the rate law holds outside the range that was measured
question   = does temperature raise the rate only up to some point
text       = every fitted arrow is fitted over a range, and the edge of the range is a question.

@record curiosity why_two_hemispheres
domain     = astronomy
unknown    = why the two hemispheres have opposite seasons at the same moment
question   = what makes summer happen in one hemisphere and winter in the other at once
text       = the question that rules out distance and points at tilt.

@record curiosity gap_in_the_periodic_table
domain     = chemistry
unknown    = what belongs in a gap the arrangement leaves open
question   = what element fills this space and what should its properties be
text       = the table predicted elements before they were found, which is a gap being read as a question.

# ============================ active learning =================================================== #
@record active_learning which_test_first
domain     = technology
context    = four hypotheses and limited time, so the cheapest experiment that halves the space wins
hypotheses = the battery is weak | 0.45 ;; the starter is failing | 0.2 ;; fuel is not reaching the engine | 0.2 ;; the oil is too thick | 0.15
experiment = watch the headlights while cranking | dim means battery | bright means not the battery ;; strip and bench test the starter | a fault means the starter | none means it is elsewhere
outcome    = watch the headlights while cranking | the lights stayed bright
note       = the headlight test costs seconds and removes the most likely hypothesis. the bench test costs an hour and removes one.
text       = the experiment worth running is the one that removes the most probability per unit of cost.

@record active_learning where_to_measure
domain     = biology
context    = the arrow is fitted over zero to six litres and the interesting question is at the edges
hypotheses = growth keeps rising with water | 0.5 ;; growth peaks and then falls with too much water | 0.5
experiment = take one reading at twelve litres | still rising means the first | lower than at six means the second
outcome    = take one reading at twelve litres | growth was lower than at six litres
note       = the informative reading is outside the measured range, not another one inside it.
text       = a sixth reading in the middle tells you almost nothing you did not have after five.

@record active_learning label_the_uncertain_ones
domain     = computing
context    = a limited budget for labelling, spent where the model is least sure
hypotheses = the model has learned this boundary | 0.5 ;; the model is guessing near this boundary | 0.5
experiment = label the examples the model scores closest to a coin flip | accuracy jumps, so the boundary was the gap | accuracy is flat, so the gap is elsewhere
outcome    = label the examples the model scores closest to a coin flip | accuracy on held out data rose sharply
text       = labelling what it already gets right buys nothing.

# ============================ research episodes ================================================= #
@record research did_the_index_help
domain     = computing
question   = did adding the index actually make the endpoint faster for users
steps      = record the median and ninety ninth percentile before ;; add the index on half the fleet ;; route matched traffic to both halves for a day ;; compare the two distributions ;; check whether writes got slower
conclusion = the read path is forty percent faster at the median and writes are six percent slower, which is worth it here
note       = the limitation is stated rather than left out: one day, one traffic mix, one region.
text       = the answer holds for the traffic that was actually measured.

@record research does_the_fertiliser_pay
domain     = economics
question   = does the extra fertiliser earn back what it costs
steps      = measure yield at six application rates on matched plots ;; price the extra yield at the local market rate ;; subtract the cost of the fertiliser at each rate ;; find where the net gain stops rising
conclusion = the gain rises to about sixty kilograms per hectare and is negative beyond a hundred
text       = more of a thing that works is not always better, and the crossing point is the finding.

@record research is_the_water_safe
domain     = medicine
question   = is the village well the source of the outbreak
steps      = map which households are ill and which well each uses ;; test water from every well for contamination ;; check whether households that switched wells stopped falling ill ;; look for an upstream source of the contamination
conclusion = illness follows one well, the water from it is contaminated, and cases stop when households switch
text       = the map, the test and the switch are three independent lines pointing at one well.

@record research why_did_accuracy_drop
domain     = computing
question   = why did the model get worse after the retrain
steps      = compare the new training data against the old for distribution shift ;; hold the data fixed and rerun the old code ;; hold the code fixed and rerun on the old data ;; bisect the change that moves the number
conclusion = the label pipeline dropped a category, so the model never saw it and could not predict it
note       = holding one side fixed at a time is what turns two suspects into one.
text       = the data changed and the code did not, and the bisect said which change did it.
